{"id": "kelly-wong-puc", "title": "Utilities chief took a contractor's gifts and handed him rival bids", "seconds": 130.5, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "688abf0668adc421", "words": 369, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "From 2012 to 2020, Harlan Kelly ran San Francisco’s water and power agency.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.96, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Public Utilities Commission", "sub": "water, power and sewers"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.6, 1.04, 1.22, 1.55, 2.63, 3.02, 3.36, 3.62, 3.84, 4.48, 4.8, 4.92, 5.25]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Walter Wong was a contractor who wanted that agency’s business.", "t0": 6.08, "t1": 9.25, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Walter Wong", "sub": "contractor, sought PUC business since 2010"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.56, 0.7, 0.8, 1.38, 1.5, 1.73, 1.91, 2.42]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "A federal jury found that Kelly took gifts from him, and handed him his rivals’ bids.", "t0": 9.37, "t1": 14.02, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Walter Wong", "sub": "contractor, sought PUC business since 2010"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.55, 0.87, 1.08, 1.24, 1.62, 1.84, 2.11, 2.33, 2.79, 3.02, 3.35, 3.48, 3.65, 4.03]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "established[7]"], "text": "This is proven in court. Kelly was convicted on six counts and cleared on two.", "t0": 14.14, "t1": 18.92, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proven in court", "sub": "convicted July 14, 2023", "chip": "Controller’s 2024 table: six of nine counts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.38, 0.86, 1.08, 2.08, 2.39, 2.54, 3.0, 3.14, 3.42, 3.79, 4.0, 4.35, 4.48]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "It starts with a vacation.", "t0": 19.14, "t1": 20.56, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2016-03-01", "to": "2016-03-31", "days": "", "fromLab": "trip to Hong Kong, Macau, China", "toLab": "Wong seeking the streetlight contract", "kicker": "The gifts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.42, 0.56, 0.63]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]", "story[1]"], "text": "In March 2016, Wong paid for the Kelly family’s trip to Hong Kong, Macau and China.", "t0": 20.68, "t1": 26.22, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2016-03-01", "to": "2016-03-31", "days": "", "fromLab": "trip to Hong Kong, Macau, China", "toLab": "Wong seeking the streetlight contract", "kicker": "The gifts"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.49, 0.78, 1.96, 2.36, 2.6, 2.72, 2.83, 3.16, 3.48, 3.7, 3.81, 4.05, 4.56, 5.02, 5.14]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "At the same time, Wong was seeking a contract to switch the City’s streetlights to LED.", "t0": 26.34, "t1": 30.93, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "A restricted source", "kicker": "The gifts", "sub": "seeking the LED streetlight contract"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.28, 0.55, 1.14, 1.42, 1.55, 1.85, 1.94, 2.46, 2.58, 2.91, 3.02, 3.33, 3.87, 4.02]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "He had sought the agency’s contracts since 2010, so Kelly couldn’t take his gifts.", "t0": 31.05, "t1": 35.97, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "A restricted source", "kicker": "The gifts", "sub": "seeking the LED streetlight contract"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.31, 0.62, 0.76, 1.23, 1.86, 2.15, 2.52, 3.36, 3.57, 3.87, 4.13, 4.32, 4.46]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "So how much were the gifts worth, in 2016 and 2017 alone?", "t0": 36.09, "t1": 40.83, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Gifts in 2016 and 2017", "kicker": "The gifts", "sub": "travel, jewelry, cash, meals"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.45, 0.66, 0.8, 0.91, 1.18, 1.59, 1.77, 2.11, 2.66, 2.77, 3.08, 3.66]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "amount"], "text": "Almost 16,000 dollars.", "t0": 40.83, "t1": 42.63, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$16,000", "label": "in gifts, almost, per the Controller", "sub": "Kelly reported none of it"}, "emph": ["Almost"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.9, 1.28]}, {"scene": "gift", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Kelly reported none of it. Wong also remodeled Kelly’s home at a discount.", "t0": 43.15, "t1": 47.53, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "A discounted remodel", "kicker": "The gifts", "sub": "about $89,000 still owed"}, "emph": ["none of it"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.77, 0.95, 1.05, 1.76, 2.09, 2.41, 2.86, 3.18, 3.38, 3.48, 3.56]}, {"scene": "bids", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Next, the bids.", "t0": 47.75, "t1": 48.99, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Rivals’ prices", "sub": "confidential"}, {"art": "magnifier", "name": "Staff scoring notes", "sub": "internal"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Walter Wong", "sub": "the bidder"}], "kicker": "The rival bids · RFP 79002 and RFP 79004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.6]}, {"scene": "bids", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "The jury found Kelly gave Wong his competitors’ prices, and the staff’s private notes rating each bidder.", "t0": 49.11, "t1": 55.36, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Rivals’ prices", "sub": "confidential"}, {"art": "magnifier", "name": "Staff scoring notes", "sub": "internal"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Walter Wong", "sub": "the bidder"}], "kicker": "The rival bids · RFP 79002 and RFP 79004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.47, 0.86, 1.2, 1.51, 1.94, 2.16, 2.79, 3.77, 3.94, 4.07, 4.52, 4.94, 5.29, 5.65, 5.89]}, {"scene": "bids", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[3]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "Here’s the twist. Wong didn’t get the streetlight contract. He withdrew his bid. The records don’t say why.", "t0": 55.48, "t1": 61.68, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Who won the streetlights?", "kicker": "The rival bids", "sub": "Wong withdrew his bid"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.33, 1.08, 1.4, 1.61, 1.74, 1.85, 2.3, 3.15, 3.31, 3.68, 3.85, 4.73, 4.93, 5.34, 5.61, 5.82]}, {"scene": "lights", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "A City review by the Controller, the City’s money watchdog, found two more deals.", "t0": 61.9, "t1": 66.14, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Holiday lights", "kicker": "The holiday lights", "sub": "Alternate Choice LLC, August 2019", "chip": "no bidding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.74, 0.87, 0.97, 1.55, 1.7, 2.04, 2.27, 2.84, 3.11, 3.32, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lights", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "In 2019, the agency bought 77 holiday light fixtures from Wong’s company, with no bidding.", "t0": 66.26, "t1": 71.97, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Holiday lights", "kicker": "The holiday lights", "sub": "Alternate Choice LLC, August 2019", "chip": "no bidding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.48, 0.92, 1.04, 1.46, 1.73, 2.36, 2.72, 2.92, 3.36, 3.59, 3.96, 4.87, 5.12, 5.32]}, {"scene": "lights", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[4]"], "text": "How much?", "t0": 72.09, "t1": 72.72, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Holiday lights", "kicker": "The holiday lights", "sub": "Alternate Choice LLC, August 2019", "chip": "no bidding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15]}, {"scene": "lights", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[4]"], "text": "43,000 dollars.", "t0": 72.72, "t1": 74.3, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$43,000", "label": "for 77 holiday light fixtures"}, "emph": ["43,000"], "wt": [0.04, 0.52, 0.84]}, {"scene": "mlok", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The second deal went to mlok consulting. Its president owned a home with Kelly.", "t0": 74.92, "t1": 79.44, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The firm’s president", "kicker": "The co-owner", "sub": "president of mlok consulting"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 0.72, 0.91, 1.06, 1.4, 2.47, 2.72, 3.19, 3.41, 3.49, 3.69, 3.86]}, {"scene": "mlok", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "He never disclosed that. How much did the City pay her firm?", "t0": 79.56, "t1": 84.03, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The firm’s president", "kicker": "The co-owner", "sub": "president of mlok consulting"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.86, 2.14, 2.32, 2.5, 2.64, 2.75, 3.03, 3.24, 3.4]}, {"scene": "mlok", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[5]"], "text": "9.5 million dollars.", "t0": 84.03, "t1": 85.56, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9.5 million", "label": "to mlok consulting as prime contractor"}, "emph": ["9.5"], "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.5, 0.75, 1.04]}, {"scene": "mlok", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The firm’s president was not charged.", "t0": 86.08, "t1": 88.03, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "disclose a personal or business relationship"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.5, 0.97, 1.17, 1.4]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "Finally, Kelly’s own mortgage.", "t0": 88.25, "t1": 89.77, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A $1.3 million refinance", "kicker": "The loan papers", "sub": "Quicken Loans"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.82, 1.01]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "With former commissioner Victor Makras, he refinanced 1.3 million dollars.", "t0": 89.89, "t1": 95.29, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A $1.3 million refinance", "kicker": "The loan papers", "sub": "Quicken Loans"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.53, 1.0, 1.28, 2.36, 2.52, 3.2, 3.44, 3.71, 3.94, 4.24]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "What did the papers hide?", "t0": 95.29, "t1": 97.03, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "A $1.3 million refinance", "kicker": "The loan papers", "sub": "Quicken Loans"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.34, 0.45, 0.8]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[6]", "established[11]"], "text": "The 89,000 dollars still owed to Wong, and a 70,000 dollar loan from Makras.", "t0": 97.03, "t1": 102.01, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["owed to Wong", "about $89,000"], "b": ["loan from Makras", "$70,000"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.71, 1.04, 1.32, 1.56, 1.76, 1.89, 2.59, 2.78, 2.87, 3.27, 3.6, 3.87, 4.15, 4.34]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[6]"], "text": "That kept the contractor’s gift out of sight. Both men were convicted of bank fraud.", "t0": 102.13, "t1": 106.97, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["owed to Wong", "about $89,000"], "b": ["loan from Makras", "$70,000"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.49, 0.6, 1.21, 1.5, 1.66, 1.78, 2.73, 3.03, 3.18, 3.33, 3.8, 3.91, 4.17]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[7]", "story[4]", "established[10]", "established[12]"], "text": "Kelly got four years in prison and a 10,000 dollar fine.", "t0": 107.19, "t1": 110.51, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Four years", "sub": "and a $10,000 fine"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.56, 0.82, 1.07, 1.19, 1.61, 1.79, 1.88, 2.12, 2.46, 2.74]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[7]", "story[4]"], "text": "An appeals court upheld it. Wong pleaded guilty, testified, and got probation.", "t0": 110.63, "t1": 115.25, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Four years", "sub": "and a $10,000 fine"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.58, 0.87, 1.26, 1.97, 2.3, 2.64, 3.03, 3.65, 3.77, 3.95]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["established[8]", "established[9]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "The Controller found no sign other staff knew.", "t0": 115.37, "t1": 117.63, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That other staff knew", "Any wrongdoing by Naomi Kelly"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.66, 0.9, 1.07, 1.42, 1.64, 1.96]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]"], "text": "Still open: exactly which bid papers were passed and when,", "t0": 117.75, "t1": 121.87, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Which bid papers were passed, and when"}, {"who": "", "what": "What mlok was paid before 2012"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 1.38, 1.9, 2.16, 2.38, 2.72, 2.88, 3.24, 3.37]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]"], "text": "and what mlok was paid before 2012.", "t0": 121.87, "t1": 124.11, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Which bid papers were passed, and when"}, {"who": "", "what": "What mlok was paid before 2012"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.47, 0.8, 0.95, 1.2, 1.5, 1.81]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "The conviction was upheld in August 2025.", "t0": 124.23, "t1": 127.15, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.52, 0.66, 1.16, 1.32, 1.64, 1.9]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.27, "t1": 129.64, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.72, 0.94, 1.27, 1.38, 1.49, 1.76, 2.01]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The case", "gift": "The gifts · almost $16,000", "bids": "The rival bids", "lights": "The holiday lights · $43,000", "mlok": "The co-owner · $9.5 million", "loan": "The loan papers", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "number"}